    "statement": "Every quartic boundary dual moment is linear in the nonzero labels theta_i=xi_iP_Z(xi_i)/lambda_i^2. Hence a valid design supplies a torus-valued kernel vector for an explicit (2e-5)(e-1) by e matrix determined before external cofactor reconstruction. Since q>e, full rank or one coloop column is an exact exclusion certificate. Deterministic e=4,5,7 controls are full rank, but no universal full-rank theorem is asserted.",
